# Jumbalaya — project context

Roguelike **jumble** word game on Love2D/Lua. Active loop: fill **pattern puzzles** from a 7-card hand, bank score × multiplier, clear 24 stages (8 sets × 3 hands). Timeline fuse → tokens; between hands → The Trade marketplace.

**Authoritative docs:** `docs/code-organization.md`, `docs/gameplay.md`, `docs/testing.md`

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `app/` | Bootstrap, lifecycle, input, persistence, engine (`app/core/`) |
| `word_game/` | Domain: `config/`, `model/`, `board/`, `ui/` |
| `word_game/ui/sidebar/` | Right-hand HUD package (stamps, deck, End Run) — use **sidebar** not vault |
| `tests/` | Headless suite — `love tests` |
| `dictionary/` | Offline word validation |
| `_tools/` | Python asset pipelines (not runtime) |
| `resources/` | Assets, shaders, sounds, fonts |
| `AlphaCardsBackup/` | Legacy Balatro reference — do not edit |

Agent docs: `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/skills/jumbalaya/SKILL.md`

## Dependency rules

- `word_game/ui/` → `app/core/` — never reverse
- `word_game/board/` — snap/geometry only (`placement/`, `jumble/`, `bonus/`); no UI imports at require time
- Cross-package: use `WORD_GAME` facade (`word_game/init.lua`), not deep `require` from `app/` or `tests/`
- Config = data; model = rules/state; ui = presentation — keep separated
- Bootstrap load order lives in `app/bootstrap.lua` only; globals (`G`, `Card`, `LayoutView`) exist after boot

## Active vs legacy

Jumble mode is the player experience (`word_game/model/jumble/`, `word_game/model/jumble_play/`). Legacy AP/plays/discards code may remain but is not active — do not extend it unless asked. Right-hand HUD is `word_game/ui/sidebar/` (`WORD_GAME.Sidebar`, `G.SIDEBAR_HUD`) — not vault.

## Verification

After logic changes: `love tests`. For structural refactors: `emmylua_check . --severity warn`. Minimize diff scope; match existing naming and patterns.
